visibility"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_0196ekW83shuTGpU9qYR6gym","tool_input":{"command":"gh repo view --json isPrivate,visibility,nameWithOwner 2>&1 | head -20","description":"Check repo visibility"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01SxCb4ZfDJrGpbW5k2qfa3A","tool_input":{"command":"gh repo view jamesponwith/spotify-recsys-ecosystem --json isPrivate,visibility,nameWithOwner","description":"Check repo visibility"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":3,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":3,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":1,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":3,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"general-purpose":3}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":106,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Bead `spot-ph0` → [PR #13](https://github.com/jamesponwith/spotify-recsys-ecosystem/pull/13)** (open, not merged)\n\n**What was wrong.** `gamut/config.py` said `depth = 100`; `cadence/config.py` says `fused_candidates = 1500`. Gamut measured the top 100 of a 1500-deep pool and published it as \"Reached by retrieval\". Nothing caught it because each file was right about itself.\n\n**What I shipped** — the mechanism, so it can't recur: depth now derives from `RetrievalConfig().fused_candidates` (the CLI held a second hand-copy of the same literal); `Collected.load(min_depth=)` refuses a cache narrower than the depth being published; the report emits a `funnel` block whose rows carry the depth they were measured at, each stage measured once and read wherever published. Tests pin the *joins* — gamut's depth against Cadence's, `SELECT_POOL` against `select()`'s `pool_size` default — not the arithmetic.\n\n**Gate:** 26 tests, ruff/format/mypy/links clean, all 18 README claims match. Green.\n\n**Review:** three lenses, 16 findings in the ledger (10 accepted, 5 deferred, 1 rejected). The sharpest caught me reintroducing the bug one row over: I'd named a stage `read_by_select`, but with a learned reranker loaded Cadence re-sorts the whole pool before `select` takes that prefix. Gamut collects reranker-free, so the row now states the configuration it measures instead of implying more.\n\n**What I did not do, and why.** Half the acceptance criteria are unmet and I left them that way deliberately. The artifact still says `depth: 100` / `10.7%`, so **the published error is still live on the page**. Regenerating needs `cadence/data` — a ~15 GB download — which no worktree has. It also can't be done in pieces: `check_claims` passes today only because the artifact *and* the README are wrong in the same way, so regenerating alone reds `make lint-all` and editing prose alone reds it the other way. Artifact and literals must move in one commit.\n\nTwo things for whoever writes it: the `0.936` floor also drifts (rerank and caps now see 1500-wide blocks; INTENT records 0.9321 at true depth, past the floor the page calls the limit of all thirteen interventions), and the \"89%\" sentence self-corrects to ~29% while the adjacent \"a hundred candidates\" literal does not. Filed as **`spot-9zd`** (P0, blocked on this, labelled `human`) with the full step list.\n\n`spot-ph0` stays open until #13 merges. Reservations released; I can't remove the worktree I'm running inside, so the spawner should reclaim it.","ttft_ms":1792,"type":"result","duration_ms":1174271,"uuid":"63debbbf-3b6a-4592-a306-3880c57eae74","ttft_stream_ms":992,"time_to_request_ms":125,"queued_turn_count":0}
